\p{The drawing follows
\citet{Figure 1.3, §1.4, p. 10}{ermentrout2010mathematical}.
The capacitor, the applied current, and three ionic branches stand
in parallel. Each branch is a conductance in series with a battery,
and the three batteries are the chloride, potassium, and sodium
reversal potentials drawn in that figure.
\citet{Figure 2.3, §2.1.3, p. 28}{izhikevich2007dynamical}
and
\citet{Figure 5.4, §5.3, draft p. 10}{dayan2001theoretical}
draw the same parallel arrangement.}
